course: dictionary
lesson: 4973
title: The prefix in- means not
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A prefix is a little group of letters added to the front of a word. It changes the meaning. The text says several prefixes mean not, and the first letter of the root often picks which one: im- before m or p (impossible, immature), il- before l (illegal, illogical), ir- before r (irregular, irresponsible), and in- for many others (incorrect, invisible).
explain: Look at incorrect. It is in- plus correct. Correct means right, so incorrect means not right, or wrong. The first letter helps too: correct starts with c, not m, p, l or r, so the prefix is in-, not im-, il- or ir-.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «The shopkeeper gave me incorrect change.» If incorrect means not right, the sentence says the change was not the right amount. That makes sense, so your meaning is good.
fact: A prefix is a group of letters added to the front of a word to change its meaning.
fact: Incorrect means not right or not true; wrong.
fact: Incorrect can also mean not suitable or not polite for the situation, as in «incorrect behaviour».
fact: The prefix in- means not in incorrect, just as un- means not in unhappy.
fact: Im-, il- and ir- are used before certain letters; in- is used for many others, like incorrect and invisible.
exercise: Sam says 7 + 5 = 13, but the answer is 12. So Sam's answer is | exactly right | correct | *incorrect | correctly
exercise: In the word incorrect, what does the prefix in- mean? | *Not | Very | Again | Before
exercise: «The shopkeeper gave me incorrect change.» What does incorrect mean here? | Given quickly with a smile | *Wrong, not the right amount | Counted twice in the shop | Too much and too kind
test: Which word uses in- to mean not? | irregular | *invisible | impossible | illegal
test: «The teacher said his behaviour was incorrect, because he shouted in class.» What does incorrect mean here? | Lost in the crowd | Happy and loud | *Not suitable or polite for the situation | Very clever
exam: Which word means not right? | invisible | incredible | intelligent | *incorrect
